# Sentry init singleton — registered-mirror exclusion baseline (FOLLOW-765).
#
# CONSUMER of the "Registered mirror files excluded from the scan" inventory
# printed by scripts/check-sentry-init-singleton.sh. Each entry is one path
# (relative to the scan root) that the gate SKIPS entirely because it is
# registered as a Rule J mirror in scripts/mirror-files.json.
#
# This is the gate's own suppression set, and it suppresses WHOLE FILES, not
# single lines — which is why it gets a committed baseline rather than a log
# line. Registering a fourth `.py` pair in scripts/mirror-files.json silently
# grew this list from 3 to 4 before FOLLOW-765; now it turns the gate RED until
# the addition is written here, in a diff a human reads.
#
# NOTE: exclusion is not blind trust. Every excluded file that holds a real
# `sentry_sdk.init(` must also carry the three FOLLOW-738 hardened markers
# (default_integrations=False, send_default_pii=False,
# include_local_variables=False) surviving the tokenizer pass, or the gate fails
# with an UNHARDENED REGISTERED MIRROR finding. This baseline governs WHICH
# files are excluded; that check governs WHETHER the exclusion is safe.
#
# TO CHANGE THIS FILE: only in the same PR that changes scripts/mirror-files.json.
# The gate prints a copy-pasteable replacement body when it fails.
#
# Current state: the FOLLOW-738 hardened initialiser — one canonical and its two
# Rule J mirrors.
count: 3
apps/data-quality/src/crons/observability.py
apps/intent-engine/src/observability.py
apps/llm-gateway/src/jobs/observability.py
